[Desktop Entry]
Type=Link
Name=Document...
Comment=Enter document name:
Icon=application-vnd.oasis.opendocument.text
URL=.source/Document.odt

# Dolphin's "Create New" menu had no office documents. KDE Frameworks compiles
# its defaults -- Folder, Text File, HTML File, Empty File and three kinds of
# link -- into the KIO library as a Qt resource (:/kio5/newfile-templates), and
# no package in trixie ships a /usr/share/templates at all: not kio, not
# libreoffice-common, not libreoffice-kf6. So an image with Writer, Calc and
# Impress installed still offered no way to start a document from the file
# manager, which is the gesture a Windows switcher reaches for first.
#
# HOW KIO READS THIS FILE (Entry::parseFile in kio's knewfilemenu.cpp):
#   Type=Link plus a URL that is neither absolute nor prefixed "__" is resolved
#   against THIS file's directory, so ".source/Document.odt" means
#   /usr/share/templates/.source/Document.odt. The KDE3 spelling "URL[$e]="
#   still parses, but nothing in Frameworks writes it any more and it buys
#   nothing here.
#   Comment= is NOT a tooltip. It is set as the label above the filename field
#   (m_label->setText(entry.comment)), so it has to read as a prompt.
#   The default filename is Name= with the ellipsis stripped and trimmed, plus
#   the extension taken from the PAYLOAD. "Document" + ".odt". Which is why
#   Name= must not itself end in ".odt", and why the payload's own basename is
#   irrelevant.
#   A dot-prefixed entry is skipped by the directory scan, so ".source" never
#   shows up as a menu item -- that is KIO's own layout, not an invention.
#   An entry whose payload is unreadable is dropped silently, so a failed build
#   step degrades to a missing menu item rather than a broken one.
#
# NO "Text File" ENTRY BELONGS IN THIS DIRECTORY. kio already compiles one in,
# and the menu is de-duplicated on the raw URL string: a copy using the same
# ".source/TextFile.txt" is silently swallowed, and a copy using any other path
# appears TWICE.
#
# The icon name is the shared-mime-info one; the Breeze icon theme carries it.
#
# The payload is written by 0550-office-templates.hook.chroot rather than
# committed. An ODF file is a ZIP; the reasoning for keeping binaries out of
# this tree is in that hook's header.

# Hand-written, not generated: tools/i18n-desktop.py only walks
# usr/share/applications, so it will neither write nor --check these keys. The
# German entry keeps the space before the ellipsis that KIO's own German
# templates use ("Textdatei ..."), so ours does not sit in the same menu looking
# like a different product wrote it.
Name[de]=Dokument …
Name[fr]=Document...
Name[es]=Documento...
Name[pt_BR]=Documento...
Name[it]=Documento...
Comment[de]=Geben Sie den Namen des Dokuments ein:
Comment[fr]=Saisissez le nom du document :
Comment[es]=Introduzca el nombre del documento:
Comment[pt_BR]=Digite o nome do documento:
Comment[it]=Inserisci il nome del documento:
